{
  "name": "KHeverest",
  "isInstrument": true,
  "explanation": "KHeverest — an eight-voice, three-oscillator hybrid polysynth modelled feature-for-feature on the Novation Peak (User Guide v1.2, read cover to cover; every control, menu page, matrix source/destination and MIDI-appendix parameter is implemented). Per voice: three oscillators with sine / triangle / sawtooth / pulse and a bank of 60 morphing wavetables (five waveforms each, swept by Shape Amount), shape modulation from Mod Env 1 and LFO 1, hard-sync 'virtual oscillator' (Vsync), saw density + density detune, fixed-note mode, per-oscillator bend range, oscillator-to-oscillator FM, ring modulator, noise with its own filter, Diverge / Drift voice character and 17 tuning tables. A resonant multimode filter (LP / BP / HP, 12 or 24 dB) with pre-filter overdrive, post-filter drive, key tracking, Amp-Env / Mod-Env-1 / LFO-1 / Osc-3 modulation and per-voice divergence; three AHDSR envelopes with hold, velocity and repeats (looping envelopes); two per-voice LFOs with phase, slew, four fade modes, repeats and common-sync plus two global LFOs, tempo sync everywhere. A 16-slot, two-source (multiplied) modulation matrix with 23 sources and 37 destinations, and a 4-slot FX matrix. Voice modes Mono / MonoLG / Mono2 / Poly / Poly2, unison up to 8 voices with detune and stereo spread, glide and pre-glide, analogue-style distortion, chorus (3 types), stereo delay (tempo sync, L/R ratio, slew), FDN reverb, 7 FX routings, and an arpeggiator with 7 modes, 1-6 octaves, swing, latch and 33 rhythm patterns. Animate buttons, pitch/mod wheels, expression pedals and CV input. 272 controls are packed into the host's 64 parameter slots; master volume, wheels and the two expression inputs are real DAW parameters, everything else automates through the matrix sources. Wavetable contents are original (only the names follow the manual).",
  "assembly": "factory/plugins/kheverest/assembly.ts",
